== neighbors.NearestCentroid: centroids, Tibshirani/ESL shrinkage recomputed, manhattan medians, priors
ok   NearestCentroid centroids_ = per-class means (exact Fraction)
ok   NearestCentroid predict = class of the nearest (Euclidean) centroid
   shrunken centroids [[4.68189, 3.401458, 4.466667], [7.392081, 4.618033, 2.772349], [3.872883, 4.4, 5.831126]]
   reference          [[4.68189, 3.401458, 4.466667], [7.392081, 4.618033, 2.772349], [3.872883, 4.4, 5.831126]]
   raw deviations [[-0.6064, -0.9336, 0.0184], [1.7197, 0.611, -1.5969], [-1.1074, 0.2548, 1.52]]
ok   NearestCentroid(shrink_threshold=0.5) centroids_ = xbar_j + m_k (s_j + s0) d'_kj with d'_kj = sign(d)(|d| - delta)_+, d_kj = (xbar_kj - xbar_j)/(m_k (s_j + s0)), m_k = sqrt(1/n_k - 1/n), s_j pooled within-class sd (n-K), s0 = median(s) (ESL eq. 18.4-18.5 as documented)
ok   NearestCentroid shrinkage: some deviations shrunk to exactly 0 (soft thresholding removes features)
ok   NearestCentroid deviations_ (1.6+) = the shrunken standardised deviations d'_kj; within_class_std_dev_ = pooled sd
   default priors='uniform': class_prior_ [0.3333333333333333, 0.3333333333333333, 0.3333333333333333] (docstring also says 'By default, the class proportions are inferred from the training data')
ok   NearestCentroid default priors='uniform' (signature 'default="uniform"') -> class_prior_ = 1/n_classes
FAIL NearestCentroid default class_prior_ = class proportions of the training data (docstring of `priors`: 'By default, the class proportions are inferred from the training data')  (got [0.3333, 0.3333, 0.3333], proportions [0.2667, 0.3333, 0.4])
ok   NearestCentroid(shrink_threshold=None) deviations_ = eq. (18.4) d_kj = (xbar_kj - xbar_j)/(m_k (s_j + s0)) unshrunk (documented 'Equal to eq. (18.4) if shrink_threshold=None')
ok   NearestCentroid(priors='empirical') class_prior_ = class counts / n
ok   NearestCentroid(priors='empirical') decision_function = -sum_j ((x_j - xbar_kj)/s_j)^2 + 2 log pi_k (ESL eq. 18.2), predict = argmax
ok   NearestCentroid(priors=[.6,.3,.1]) uses the given priors in the discriminant
ok   NearestCentroid(priors=[.7,.7,.1]) not summing to 1 -> normalised with a warning
ok   NearestCentroid(metric='manhattan') centroids_ = feature-wise medians (documented; even counts -> midpoint)
ok   NearestCentroid(metric='manhattan') predict = argmin of the L1 distance to the medians
ok   NearestCentroid(shrink_threshold) with a single-sample class: m_k = sqrt(1/1 - 1/n) finite, fits
